+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are only visible with the
+`-l`/`--links` flag. Without it they are skipped, with a notice naming
+the flag.
+
+With `--links` a symbolic link is shown as a file whose name is the
+link's name plus `.rclonelink`, whose size is the length of the link
+target, and whose contents are the link target. This is the same
+convention the [local backend](/local/) uses, so copying out of an
+archive to a backend which supports symlinks recreates them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A symlink must be named with the `.rclonelink` suffix, as with the
+local backend, e.g. `:archive:/tmp/test.zip/src/link.txt.rclonelink`.
+A regular file in the archive whose name happens to end in
+`.rclonelink` stays a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
